attribution: Children's game song (warabe uta) thought to date from the Edo period, words anonymous; the form sung today was written down and arranged by Nagayo Motoori (died 1945) and was on record by about 1920. Melody and words are public domain. The tune uses a Japanese pentatonic scale and comes to rest on A rather than on the keynote.
source_url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tōryanse
tags: japan, children, game song, pentatonic, crosswalk

